preConditionHook:
// Brooks's single-bar test for a breakout bar likely to follow through: a
// with-trend body of at least bodyFraction of the bar's range, and BOTH tails
// no larger than tailFraction of it. Bare single-bar OHLC arithmetic, so no
// hook state -- the whole rule is the conditions.
//
// The tails are the difference from the catalog's CloseRangePosition, which
// only places the closing price inside the range: a shaved-top bull bar with a small
// body passes that and fails this. bodyFraction 0.6 / tailFraction 0.15 are
// the majority readings across the Brooks corpus (0.5 and 0.7 also appear for
// the body, 0.2 for the tails); both are meant to be optimized.
//
// lag follows InsideBar's convention so the several sources that test the
// PRIOR bar use this rule at lag 1 rather than a second rule.
